<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haji Kerantukh Berzeg</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hajji Berzeg Kerandeqo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haji Kerantukh Berzeg was an Ubykh leader of the Berzeg family and one of the principal commanders of Circassian resistance to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>. In 1861 he presided over the Circassian assembly at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sochi">Sochi</a>, which sought support from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. After the Russian conquest of 1864 he went into exile in the Ottoman Empire with the entire Ubykh people.</p></div>
